/**
 * The resolution a settlement carries, or `undefined` when it carries none.
 *
 * `PiSettlementResolution` makes an ill-formed resolution inexpressible, and a
 * type reaches exactly as far as the compiler: this event crosses a process
 * boundary as JSON, so the same rule is applied here, where it can actually be
 * enforced. This MIRRORS the type rather than approximating it — validating
 * the two fields separately let both of them be well-formed and still say the
 * thing the type forbids, `{status: "idle", runActive: true}`, which is the
 * contradiction the coupling exists to remove. Only a run the thread still
 * holds open can be writing a group, and that run is what keeps the status
 * `running`.
