 * `createThread` does not answer until the message it carries has been
 * admitted, so the thread has no id while Pi is holding the prompt — and a
 * command that raises a dialog would then be waiting on a client that cannot
 * subscribe to it, forever. Nothing here can tell an interactive command from
 * a quiet one, so all of them are excluded from that one position.
 *
