/**
 * A send that did not get through, and the attempt it did not get through
 * with.
 *
 * A host that wants to hand a refused prompt back has to be HANDED it. The
 * composer empties itself before the runtime is called
 * (`BaseComposerRuntimeCore.send`) and the core swallows the rejection
 * (`sendTask.catch(() => {})`), so by the time the failure lands the composer
 * holds whatever has been typed since and the converted attachments are gone.
 * Reading either of them back is reading the wrong thing.
 *
 * The payload is captured at send time and never changes, and it names its
 * OWNER, so a refusal cannot be applied to a composer that did not produce it.
 */
