// decision:: the field KEEPS Pi's meaning, passed through as Pi sends it.
// The two alternatives are worse. Redefining it as "the compaction took
// effect" would make this adapter say something about the wire that the
// wire does not say, and every future reading of Pi's own logs would
// disagree with it. Dropping it breaks consumers for no gain, since a
// passthrough field that is accurate about Pi costs nothing to carry. So
// the rule is: read the transcript, not this flag.

