cases.new_string:
export const piClient = createPiNodeClient({
  workspacePath: process.env.PI_WORKSPACE_PATH ?? process.cwd(),
  // agentDir?: override Pi's config dir (default ~/.pi/agent)
  // model?:    a resolved Pi `Model` to seed new sessions (see Model controls)
});
```

#### Host configuration

A local example can stop at `workspacePath`. A deployed host owns more, and
every option below is read by create, resume, the catalog and the snapshot
alike — configuring one of them in isolation is what leaks.

| Option                 | What it does                                                                                                             |
| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `sessionsDir`          | The session store for create, list and lookup. Sessions survive a restart because all three read the same directory.       |
| `agentDir`             | Pi's config dir. Also where the model runtime reads `auth.json` and `models.json`, so nothing touches the host's `~/.pi`.   |
| `lockWorkspace`        | Refuse any call naming a workspace other than `workspacePath`. A deployed host serves one directory.                        |
| `modelRuntime`         | The one `ModelRuntime` behind the catalog, `setModel`, readiness and every session. Supply it to share a runtime-only key.   |
| `model`                | The model new sessions open on. A resumed session keeps the model it was saved with.                                        |
| `thinkingLevel`        | The thinking level new sessions open on, same rule.                                                                        |
| `scopedModels`         | The models this host offers. They become the whole catalog and the only models `setModel` accepts.                          |
| `createResourceLoader` | Build one session's `ResourceLoader`, called with its id before Pi builds the session.                                      |

`getPiThreadSupervisor().getRunningThreadCount()` reports how many sessions are
mid-run, for a deploy that waits for the host to go idle.

A runtime-only API key never reaches disk:

```ts
const modelRuntime = await ModelRuntime.create({
  authPath: `${agentDir}/auth.json`,
  modelsPath: `${agentDir}/models.json`,
});
await modelRuntime.setRuntimeApiKey("openrouter", process.env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY!);
