`createResourceLoader` composes rather than replaces. Pi's
`appendSystemPromptOverride` receives the prompts the loader discovered, so
return `[...base, mine]`; returning `[mine]` drops every discovered prompt.

```ts
createResourceLoader: async ({ threadId, workspacePath }) => {
  const loader = new DefaultResourceLoader({
    cwd: workspacePath,
    agentDir,
    appendSystemPromptOverride: (base) => [...base, `Session id: ${threadId}.`],
  });
  await loader.reload();
  return loader;
};
